  {
   "type": "Questions",
   "props": {
    "id": "Questions-42",
    "band": "sunk",
    "blocks": [
     {
      "type": "Title",
      "props": {
       "id": "Title-37",
       "html": "String quartet questions",
       "tag": "h2",
       "cls": "h3"
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Paragraph",
      "props": {
       "id": "Paragraph-38",
       "html": "Have a question about substitutions or other booking details? You’ll find the answers on our <a href=\"/planners/faq/\">full list of questions</a>. Want to know more about the four instruments, or how a trio or duo compares? Check out our <a href=\"/blog/what-is-a-string-quartet/\">guide to the string quartet</a>.",
       "cls": "note"
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Faq",
      "props": {
       "id": "Faq-39",
       "items": [
        {
         "q": "What does a string quartet cost for a wedding in Denver?",
         "a": "A Denver wedding guide puts a classical string duo or trio for a ceremony or cocktail hour at $800 to $2,000, and a full quartet costs more. That’s a general view of what strings cost in the Denver, Colorado market. Just send us the date, the venue and the size you’re picturing, and we’ll come back with a price."
        },
        {
         "q": "Can a string quartet play outdoors?",
         "a": "Yes. We’ll just need shade, cover from rain and level ground, since violins can’t sit in direct sun or get wet. Cold weather matters, too, since strings go out of tune and fingers slow down once it drops into the fifties, so for a mountain ceremony we’ll work out a backup plan with you in case it gets cold."
        },
        {
         "q": "How loud is a string quartet?",
         "a": "It’s about as loud as a conversation at the next table. Indoors, a quartet can play a ceremony or a cocktail hour with nothing plugged in. Outdoors, or in a large hall where everyone needs to hear the officiant, we can bring a small sound system, and the musicians will adjust the volume to fit the space."
        },
        {
         "q": "Can you play a song that isn't on the list?",
         "a": "Yes. We can usually have a new song written out for your group, whether that’s one violin or a full quartet. Send the title with the date, and a recording of the version you mean if there's more than one."
        },
        {
         "q": "Who will the musicians be?",
         "a": "They’ll be string players from our roster, and we’ll let you know their names when you book."
        }
       ],
       "schema": true
      }
     },
     {
      "type": "Paragraph",
      "props": {
       "id": "Paragraph-40",
       "html": "We quote each date one-by-one.",
       "cls": "note"
      }
